{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_a98464d6416d4f279e2e19c4","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 110 lines\n1: # DaoJing canonical CBOR fixtures v1: errata\n2: \n3: Status: RATIFIED J1 ERRATA (architect sign-off 2026-09-22)\n4: \n5: This additive errata is ratified for J1 and J2. The frozen corpus remains\n6: unchanged; these entries define codec policy, host-capability refusals, and\n7: the corrected per-host test obligations.\n8: \n9: This file is additive. `cbor-v1.json`, `cbor-v1.README.md` and\n10: `cbor-v1.generate.py` are frozen and unedited. Nothing here changes a\n11: frozen byte, a frozen case, or a frozen refusal class of a frozen case. It\n12: records what the J1 JVM/Node codec (`dao.jing.cbor`) found while running the\n13: corpus, and the codec policies that J2 (Dart) must mirror. Each entry took\n14: effect for the README when the architect ratified it.\n15: \n16: Recorded 2026-09-22 by claude-opus-5 (J1 and the J1 review fixes), from the\n17: J1 reviews by qwen3.8-max and deepseek-v4-pro.\n18: \n19: ## E1. Corrected per-host N/A table (README Obligations)\n20: \n21: The README table assumed raw host numbers. The corpus input language builds\n22: carriers (float64, decimal and rational carriers on Node; the Rational\n23: carrier for denominator 1 on the JVM), which host collections do not merge\n24: with native numbers. Observed in J1:\n25: \n26: | Case | JVM | Node |\n27: |---|---|---|\n28: | `coll/map-int-float-key-collapse` | live, refused | live, refused |\n29: | `coll/set-float-decimal-collapse` | live, refused | live, refused |\n30: | `coll/set-signed-zero-collapse` | N/A (merged) | live, refused |\n31: | `coll/set-int-ratio-collapse` | live, refused | live, refused |\n32: | `coll/set-decimal-scale-collapse` | N/A (merged) | live, refused |\n33: | `coll/set-vector-list-collapse` | N/A (merged) | N/A (merged) |\n34: | `coll/map-integer-width-duplicate` | N/A (merged) | live, refused |\n35: | `coll/set-nan-payload-duplicate` | live, refused | N/A (merged) |\n36: | `coll/map-nan-payload-duplicate` | live, refused | N/A (merged) |\n37: \n38: \"live, refused\" means the host held both members and the codec refused with\n39: the frozen class. The README rows it corrects: the JVM holds\n40: `set-int-ratio-collapse` and both NaN-payload cases; Node holds\n41: `map-int-float-key-collapse`, `set-float-decimal-collapse`,\n42: `set-signed-zero-collapse`, `set-int-ratio-collapse` and\n43: `set-decimal-scale-collapse`. The J1 tests skip a case only when it is in\n44: this table's N/A column for the host and the host really merged its members;\n45: any other merge fails. Dart is not yet observed (J2).\n46: \n47: ## E2. A host-capability refusal class: `host-collapse`\n48: \n49: A J1 class outside the frozen 16. It is raised by decode when building a\n50: host map or set would merge members that Jing's portable equality keeps\n51: distinct, so the value cannot be held without losing an entry.\n52: \n53: Scope: ClojureScript map keys and set elements that are keywords or symbols\n54: whose joined names collide, for example `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` and\n55: `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")`: ClojureScript compares both keywords and symbols by\n56: the joined name (observed on Node in J1; a J1 review had assumed symbols\n57: compare by fields, and they do not). Identifier values in vectors and lists\n58: are unaffected. The JVM compares identifiers by fields and is unaffected;\n59: Dart is to be checked in J2.\n60: \n61: Corpus effect: canonical `coll/map-both-slash-keywords` cannot be held on\n62: Node. Decoding it there refuses with `host-collapse`, and the J1 test skips\n63: its encode by id while a Node-only test proves the limitation. Jing's\n64: acceptance rules themselves stay host-independent: this class reports a\n65: host data-model limit, not a different acceptance decision.\n66: \n67: ## E3. Decimal exponent window\n68: \n69: Every host accepts a decimal (tag 4) exactly when its exponent lies in\n70: \n71:     [-2147483647, 2147483648]   i.e.  [-(2^31 - 1), 2^31]\n72: \n73: which is the JVM `BigDecimal` window (scale = -exponent is a 32-bit int).\n74: Outside it the value is refused `malformed-number`, on encode (the\n75: `decimal` constructor) and on decode. Node mirrors the window exactly\n76: (`decimal-exponent-min` / `decimal-exponent-max` in `dao.jing.cbor`); Dart\n77: must too. Test bytes, tag 4 over `[exponent 1]`:\n78: \n79: | Hex | Exponent | Outcome |\n80: |---|---|---|\n81: | `c4821a8000000001` | 2^31 | accepted |\n82: | `c4821a8000000101` | 2^31 + 1 | `malformed-number` |\n83: | `c4823a7ffffffe01` | -(2^31 - 1) | accepted |\n84: | `c4823a7fffffff01` | -2^31 | `malformed-number` |\n85: \n86: The frozen corpus pins no exponent window (README A12 rules only bignum\n87: exponents out), so this is codec policy, not a corpus change.\n88: \n89: ## E4. Maximum nesting depth\n90: \n91: `max-depth` is 128, a J1 policy, ratified. The top-level item is\n92: at depth 1 and every array, map and tag puts its contents one level deeper;\n93: a list frame (tag 27 over `[name items]`) therefore costs three levels.\n94: Decode refuses deeper nesting `malformed-cbor` before recursing; encode\n95: refuses it `unsupported-value`. Both count the same CBOR depth, so anything\n96: encode emits, decode accepts. No corpus payload nests beyond a handful of\n97: levels. The limit exists so a hostile payload (for example 10 000 nested\n98: arrays) is refused instead of overflowing the host stack.\n99: \n100: ## E5. Notes for the architect\n101: \n102: - Collapse checking groups members by `equiv-hash` and compares pairwise\n103:   within a group. That is worst-case O(n^2) in collection size, bounded by\n104:   the input and reachable only with crafted hash collisions. Recorded, not\n105:   changed.\n106: - `num-hash` and `equiv-hash` values are host-specific: the keys they hash\n107:   are host-independent, but the JVM hashes strings with Murmur3 and\n108:   ClojureScript with another scheme. Hash values are for use within one\n109:   host and must never cross hosts; anything that partitions by hash across\n110:   hosts (published-index sharding, for example) needs a specified digest."}],"deferred":false}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_095207b6137540d59c2ec76a","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 453 lines\n1: (ns dao.jing.cbor-test\n2:   \"`dao.jing.cbor` against the frozen corpus (J1 JVM and Node, J2 Dart).\n3: \n4:    Every corpus case runs on each host: canonical inputs encode to the\n5:    frozen hex and digest and the frozen hex decodes back to an equal value;\n6:    encode and decode refusals raise the frozen class. A case is skipped only\n7:    by id, with its reason, and only where the README (or a recorded host\n8:    limitation reported with this phase) says the host cannot build the\n9:    input. The remaining tests prove the effective Boring options (JVM and\n10:    Node), byte isolation, independence from print settings, the hardening\n11:    limits, and the portable numeric operations, on every host.\"\n12:   (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n13:             [dao.jing :as jing]\n14:             [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n15:             [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as fx]\n16:             #?@(:cljd []\n17:                 :default [[boring.core :as boring]\n18:                           [dao.jing.cbor.boring :as cbor-boring]]))\n19:   #?@(:cljd [(:import [\"dart:core\" BigInt])]))\n20: \n21: \n22: (def host\n23:   #?(:cljd :dart :clj :jvm :cljs :node))\n24: \n25: \n26: (def skip-by-id\n27:   \"Cases this host cannot build at all, with the reason.\"\n28:   {:jvm {\"num/js-unsafe-integer\"\n29:          \"README Obligations: applies to Node only; N/A on JVM and Dart\"}\n30:    :node {\"host/character\"\n31:           \"ClojureScript has no character type: a char literal is a string\"\n32:           \"host/nested-in-vector\"\n33:           \"its unsupported member is a character; ClojureScript has none\"\n34:           \"coll/map-both-slash-keywords\"\n35:           (str \"ClojureScript keyword equality compares the joined name, so\"\n36:                \" (keyword nil \\\"a/b\\\") and (keyword \\\"a\\\" \\\"b\\\") are one map\"\n37:                \" key: the host cannot hold this value (reported as a\"\n38:                \" J1 finding)\")}\n39:    :dart {\"host/character\"\n40:           \"Dart has no character type: a char literal is a string\"\n41:           \"host/nested-in-vector\"\n42:           \"its unsupported member is a character; Dart has none\"\n43:           \"num/js-unsafe-integer\"\n44:           \"README Obligations: applies to Node only; N/A on JVM and Dart\"}})\n45: \n46: \n47: (def collapse-not-applicable\n48:   \"Encode-side collapse and duplicate refusals whose members this host's\n49:    constructor was observed to merge (cbor-v1.errata.md corrects the\n50:    README table this way). Such a case is skipped only when the host\n51:    really merged the members; a case not listed here must refuse, so a\n52:    regression that starts merging fails instead of skipping.\"\n53:   {:jvm #{\"coll/set-signed-zero-collapse\" \"coll/set-decimal-scale-collapse\"\n54:           \"coll/set-vector-list-collapse\" \"coll/map-integer-width-duplicate\"}\n55:    :node #{\"coll/set-vector-list-collapse\" \"coll/set-nan-payload-duplicate\"\n56:            \"coll/map-nan-payload-duplicate\"}\n57:    :dart #{\"coll/set-signed-zero-collapse\" \"coll/set-vector-list-collapse\"}})\n58: \n59: \n60: (defn- skip!\n61:   [id reason]\n62:   (println (str \"SKIP \" (name host) \" \" id \": \" reason)))\n63: \n64: \n65: (defn- refusal-of\n66:   \"The refusal class keyword f throws, ::none, or [::other message].\"\n67:   [f]\n68:   (try (f)\n69:        ::none\n70:        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n71:          (or (cbor/refusal e)\n72:              [::other #?(:cljd (str e)\n73:                          :clj (str (type e) \" \" (ex-message e))\n74:                          :cljs (str e))]))))\n75: \n76: \n77: (defn- guarded\n78:   \"Run one case, reporting an unexpected throw as a failure of that case\n79:    rather than aborting the whole corpus loop.\"\n80:   [id f]\n81:   (try (f)\n82:        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n83:          (is false (str id \" threw \" #?(:cljd (str e) :default (ex-message e)))))))\n84: \n85: \n86: (defn- hex-of\n87:   [bs]\n88:   (fx/bytes->hex bs))\n89: \n90: \n91: ;; ==========================================================================\n92: ;; The corpus\n93: ;; ==========================================================================\n94: \n95: (deftest canonical-cases-encode-and-round-trip\n96:   (doseq [c (fx/cases-of-kind \"canonical\")\n97:           :let [id (get c \"id\")\n98:                 skip (get-in skip-by-id [host id])]]\n99:     (if skip\n100:       (skip! id skip)\n101:       (guarded\n102:         id\n103:         #(testing id\n104:            (let [v (fx/input->value (get c \"input\"))\n105:                  bs (cbor/encode v)]\n106:              (is (= (get c \"hex\") (hex-of bs)) \"encodes to the frozen bytes\")\n107:              (is (= (get c \"sha256\") (jing/sha256-bytes bs)) \"frozen digest\")\n108:              (let [back (cbor/decode (fx/hex->bytes (get c \"hex\")))]\n109:                (is (= (get c \"hex\") (hex-of (cbor/encode back)))\n110:                    \"decoded value re-encodes to the frozen bytes\")\n111:                (is (cbor/equiv v back) \"decoded value equals the input\"))))))))\n112: \n113: \n114: (deftest encode-refusal-cases-refuse-with-the-frozen-class\n115:   ;; Unexpected host merges and unbuildable inputs are collected and\n116:   ;; asserted once at the end: on Dart a failing `is` throws, and one early\n117:   ;; failure must not hide the rest of the corpus.\n118:   (let [unexpected (atom [])]\n119:     (doseq [c (fx/cases-of-kind \"encode-refusal\")\n120:             :let [id (get c \"id\")\n121:                   skip (get-in skip-by-id [host id])]]\n122:       (if skip\n123:         (skip! id skip)\n124:         (guarded\n125:           id\n126:           #(let [input (get c \"input\")\n127:                  built (refusal-of (fn [] (fx/input->value input)))\n128:                  v (when (= ::none built) (fx/input->value input))\n129:                  n (fx/dsl-member-count input)]\n130:              (cond\n131:                ;; The portable constructors are part of the codec: a\n132:                ;; ratio with denominator 0 is refused when it is built.\n133:                (not= ::none built)\n134:                (is (= (keyword (get c \"refusal\")) built) id)\n135: \n136:                (not (fx/constructible? v))\n137:                (swap! unexpected conj [id :not-constructible])\n138: \n139:                (and n (< (count v) n))\n140:                (if (contains? (collapse-not-applicable host) id)\n141:                  (skip! id \"host constructor merged the members (N/A; cbor-v1.errata.md E1)\")\n142:                  (do (println (str \"MERGED \" (name host) \" \" id))\n143:                      (swap! unexpected conj [id :host-merged])))\n144: \n145:                :else\n146:                (is (= (keyword (get c \"refusal\")) (refusal-of (fn [] (cbor/encode v))))\n147:                    id))))))\n148:     (is (empty? @unexpected)\n149:         (str \"not an N/A row for \" (name host) \": \" (pr-str @unexpected)))))\n150: \n151: \n152: (deftest decode-refusal-cases-refuse-with-the-frozen-class\n153:   (doseq [c (fx/cases-of-kind \"decode-refusal\")\n154:           :let [id (get c \"id\")]]\n155:     (guarded\n156:       id\n157:       #(is (= (keyword (get c \"refusal\"))\n158:               (refusal-of (fn [] (cbor/decode (fx/hex->bytes (get c \"hex\"))))))\n159:            id))))\n160: \n161: \n162: (deftest groups-hold-on-produced-bytes\n163:   (let [produced (into {}\n164:                        (keep (fn [c]\n165:                                (let [id (get c \"id\")]\n166:                                  (when-not (get-in skip-by-id [host id])\n167:                                    [id (hex-of (cbor/encode\n168:                                                  (fx/input->value (get c \"input\"))))]))))\n169:                        (fx/cases-of-kind \"canonical\"))\n170:         cases (filter #(contains? produced (get % \"id\")) (fx/cases-of-kind \"canonical\"))]\n171:     (doseq [[g members] (group-by #(get % \"equivalence\") cases)\n172:             :when g]\n173:       (is (= 1 (count (set (map #(produced (get % \"id\")) members)))) g))\n174:     (doseq [[g members] (reduce (fn [acc c]\n175:                                   (reduce #(update %1 %2 (fnil conj []) c)\n176:                                           acc (get c \"distinct\")))\n177:                                 {} cases)]\n178:       (is (= (count members) (count (set (map #(produced (get % \"id\")) members))))\n179:           g))))\n180: \n181: \n182: #?(:cljs\n183:    (deftest cljs-cannot-hold-slash-crossed-identifier-keys\n184:      ;; Evidence for the coll/map-both-slash-keywords skip: ClojureScript\n185:      ;; keyword equality compares the joined name, so the host merges the\n186:      ;; two keys, and decode refuses rather than silently losing one.\n187:      (let [c (fx/case-by-id \"coll/map-both-slash-keywords\")]\n188:        (is (= 1 (count (fx/input->value (get c \"input\")))))\n189:        (is (= (symbol nil \"a/b\") (symbol \"a\" \"b\"))\n190:            \"cbor-v1.errata.md E2: ClojureScript symbols also compare by joined name\")\n191:        (is (= :host-collapse\n192:               (refusal-of #(cbor/decode (fx/hex->bytes (get c \"hex\")))))))))\n193: \n194: \n195: (deftest slash-crossed-symbol-set-is-held-or-refused-never-merged\n196:   ;; #{(symbol \"a\" \"b\") (symbol nil \"a/b\")}: canonical bytes, distinct\n197:   ;; under portable equality. The JVM holds both; ClojureScript cannot\n198:   ;; and refuses host-collapse (cbor-v1.errata.md E2), never losing one.\n199:   (let [frame \"d81b826f64616f2e6a696e672f73796d626f6c82\"\n200:         hex (str \"d9010282\" frame \"61616162\" frame \"f663612f62\")]\n201:     (is (= #?(:cljd ::none :clj ::none :cljs :host-collapse)\n202:            (refusal-of #(cbor/decode (fx/hex->bytes hex)))))))\n203: \n204: \n205: ;; ==========================================================================\n206: ;; Effective Boring options and one-item payloads\n207: ;; ==========================================================================\n208: \n209: (defn- concat-bytes\n210:   [a b]\n211:   (fx/hex->bytes (str (hex-of a) (hex-of b))))\n212: \n213: \n214: #?(:cljd nil\n215:    :default\n216:    (deftest boring-profile-options-are-locked\n217:      (is (= {:profile :canonical :stringref false :shapes false} cbor-boring/opts))\n218:      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default)\n219:            (boring/encode 1 (assoc cbor-boring/opts :stringref true)))\n220:          \"stringref cannot be switched on under :canonical\")\n221:      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default)\n222:            (boring/encode 1 (assoc cbor-boring/opts :shapes true)))\n223:          \"shapes cannot be switched on under :canonical\")))\n224: \n225: \n226: (deftest payloads-are-one-item-then-end\n227:   (let [v {:xs [\"abc\" \"abc\" \"abc\"] :m [{:a 1 :b 2} {:a 3 :b 4}]}\n228:         bs (cbor/encode v)\n229:         h (hex-of bs)]\n230:     (is (cbor/equiv v (cbor/decode bs)))\n231:     (is (not (re-find #\"d90100|d819\" h)) \"no stringref tags\")\n232:     (is (= :trailing-data (refusal-of #(cbor/decode (concat-bytes bs bs)))))\n233:     (is (= :trailing-data\n234:            (refusal-of #(cbor/decode (concat-bytes bs (cbor/encode {\"index\" 0})))))\n235:         \"an index-like frame after the item is trailing data, never skipped\")))\n236: \n237: \n238: ;; ==========================================================================\n239: ;; Byte isolation and print independence\n240: ;; ==========================================================================\n241: \n242: (defn- set-byte!\n243:   [bs i v]\n244:   #?(:cljd (. bs \"[]=\" i v)\n245:      :clj (aset-byte bs i (unchecked-byte v))\n246:      :cljs (aset bs i v)))\n247: \n248: \n249: (deftest byte-strings-are-isolated-from-mutation\n250:   (let [input (fx/hex->bytes \"0102030405\")\n251:         encoded (cbor/encode input)\n252:         before (hex-of encoded)]\n253:     (set-byte! input 0 9)\n254:     (is (= before (hex-of encoded)) \"mutating the input leaves the payload\")\n255:     (is (= before (hex-of (cbor/encode (fx/hex->bytes \"0102030405\")))))\n256:     (let [decoded (cbor/decode encoded)]\n257:       (set-byte! decoded 1 9)\n258:       (is (= \"0102030405\" (hex-of (cbor/decode encoded)))\n259:           \"mutating a decoded array leaves the payload and later decodes\")\n260:       (let [again (cbor/decode encoded)]\n261:         (set-byte! encoded 5 9)\n262:         (is (= \"0102030405\" (hex-of again))\n263:             \"mutating the payload leaves an earlier decoded array\")))))\n264: \n265: \n266: (deftest encoding-ignores-ambient-print-settings\n267:   (let [cases (fx/cases-of-kind \"canonical\")]\n268:     (doseq [c cases\n269:             :let [id (get c \"id\")]\n270:             :when (not (get-in skip-by-id [host id]))]\n271:       (let [v (fx/input->value (get c \"input\"))]\n272:         (is (= (get c \"hex\")\n273:                (hex-of (binding [*print-length* 1\n274:                                  *print-level* 1\n275:                                  *print-meta* true\n276:                                  #?@(:clj [*print-dup* true\n277:                                            *print-namespace-maps* true])]\n278:                          (cbor/encode v))))\n279:             id)))))\n280: \n281: \n282: ;; ==========================================================================\n283: ;; Portable numeric operations\n284: ;; ==========================================================================\n285: \n286: (defn- big\n287:   [s]\n288:   #?(:cljd (BigInt.parse s) :clj (bigint s) :cljs (js/BigInt s)))\n289: \n290: \n291: (def ones\n292:   [1 (big \"1\") (cbor/float64 1) (cbor/decimal 0 1) (cbor/decimal -1 10)\n293:    (cbor/decimal -2 100) (cbor/ratio 1 1)])\n294: \n295: \n296: (deftest equal-values-compare-zero-and-hash-alike-both-ways\n297:   (doseq [a ones b ones]\n298:     (is (cbor/num= a b) (pr-str [a b]))\n299:     (is (zero? (cbor/num-compare a b)) (pr-str [a b]))\n300:     (is (= (cbor/num-hash a) (cbor/num-hash b)) (pr-str [a b])))\n301:   (let [zeros [0 (cbor/float64 0) (cbor/float64 -0.0) (cbor/decimal -3 0)\n302:                (cbor/ratio 0 5)]]\n303:     (doseq [a zeros b zeros]\n304:       (is (cbor/num= a b) (pr-str [a b]))\n305:       (is (= (cbor/num-hash a) (cbor/num-hash b))))))\n306: \n307: \n308: (deftest order-is-exact-and-total\n309:   (let [nan (cbor/float64-from-bits \"7ff8000000000000\")\n310:         ladder [(cbor/float64-from-bits \"fff0000000000000\")\n311:                 (cbor/float64 -1e308)\n312:                 (big \"-100000000000000000000000\")\n313:                 -1\n314:                 (cbor/ratio -1 3)\n315:                 0\n316:                 (cbor/ratio 1 10)\n317:                 (cbor/float64 0.1)\n318:                 (cbor/decimal -1 2)\n319:                 1\n320:                 (big \"9007199254740992\")\n321:                 (big \"9007199254740993\")\n322:                 (cbor/float64 1e308)\n323:                 (cbor/float64-from-bits \"7ff0000000000000\")\n324:                 nan]]\n325:     (doseq [[i a] (map-indexed vector ladder)\n326:             [j b] (map-indexed vector ladder)]\n327:       (is (= (compare i j) (cbor/num-compare a b)) (pr-str [a b])))\n328:     (is (cbor/num= nan (cbor/float64-from-bits \"7ff8000000000001\")))\n329:     (is (not (cbor/num= (cbor/float64 0.1) (cbor/ratio 1 10)))\n330:         \"0.1 as a float is its exact binary value, not one tenth\")\n331:     (is (cbor/num= (cbor/decimal -1 1) (cbor/ratio 1 10)))\n332:     (is (= 1 (cbor/num-compare (big \"9007199254740993\")\n333:                                (cbor/float64 9007199254740992)))\n334:         \"no rounding through double\")))\n335: \n336: \n337: (deftest kinds-survive-encoding\n338:   (doseq [[a b] [[1 (cbor/float64 1)] [1 (cbor/ratio 1 1)]\n339:                  [(cbor/decimal 0 1) (cbor/decimal -1 10)]\n340:                  [(cbor/float64 0) (cbor/float64 -0.0)]]]\n341:     (is (cbor/num= a b))\n342:     (is (not= (hex-of (cbor/encode a)) (hex-of (cbor/encode b)))\n343:         \"numeric equality never merges content identity\")\n344:     (is (= (hex-of (cbor/encode b)) (hex-of (cbor/encode (cbor/decode (cbor/encode b))))))))\n345: \n346: \n347: (deftest collections-recurse-through-portable-equality\n348:   (let [a [1 {:k (cbor/float64 1)} #{(cbor/decimal -1 10)}]\n349:         b (list (cbor/ratio 1 1) {:k 1} #{(cbor/decimal 0 1)})]\n350:     (is (cbor/equiv a b))\n351:     (is (cbor/equiv b a))\n352:     (is (= (cbor/equiv-hash a) (cbor/equiv-hash b))))\n353:   (is (not (cbor/equiv [1] [2])))\n354:   (is (not (cbor/equiv (keyword nil \"a/b\") (keyword \"a\" \"b\")))\n355:       \"identifiers compare by their fields\")\n356:   (is (not (cbor/equiv \"1\" 1))))\n357: \n358: \n359: ;; ==========================================================================\n360: ;; Hardening: nesting depth, the decimal exponent window, number guards\n361: ;; ==========================================================================\n362: \n363: (defn- nested-vector\n364:   \"k vectors nested inside each other: CBOR depth k.\"\n365:   [k]\n366:   (reduce (fn [acc _] [acc]) [] (range (dec k))))\n367: \n368: \n369: (defn- nested-list\n370:   \"k lists nested inside each other: CBOR depth 3k.\"\n371:   [k]\n372:   (reduce (fn [acc _] #?(:cljd (with-meta (list acc) nil) :default (list acc)))\n373:           ()\n374:           (range (dec k))))\n375: \n376: \n377: (def ^:private list-open\n378:   \"tag 27, [\\\"dao.jing/list\\\" ...: the bytes opening