{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_ec44a545424c463299bdf620","toolName":"grep","result":[{"type":"text","text":"collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:29:The only cross-phase production edit should be to a namespace created by this unit: J1 creates the shared `dao.jing.cbor` facade, and J2 fills in its `:cljd` implementation route. No pre-existing source file needs modification.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-30-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-31-Neither owner gate blocks this unit. The first prohibited crossing is step 3, when the new codec becomes the address source, backends change to opaque bytes, and portable numeric semantics enter `dao.space`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-32-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-33-One plan correction must be incorporated in the new implementation: Boring 0.1.30 does not reliably expose array-payload tag-27 frames as `boring.data/UnknownRecord`; that carrier is associated with record-shaped/map payloads. The wrapper must use `:on-unknown-record` to create a private tagged sentinel and then perform closed Jing name-and-shape dispatch. This stays within the new codec namespace and does not require an existing-code edit.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-34-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-35-This first unit can prove codec-level requirements, including portable numeric operations directly. It cannot claim the whole epic’s acceptance yet. Backend isolation, address-mismatch handling, file migration, remote/DHT agreement, and actual `dao.space` consumer behavior belong to steps 3–5.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-36-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-37-## 2. Bounded work package as phases\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-38-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-39-A J0–J3 split is preferable to combining fixtures and implementation. It preserves the plan’s requirement that the contract be frozen before implementation and gives reviewers small, causally clear diffs.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-40-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-41-### J0 — Freeze the encoding contract\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-42-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-43-Proposed file box:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-44-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-45-- New `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-46-- New `test/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-47-- New fixture provenance document beside the resource, for example `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.README.md`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-48-- No production source changes\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-49-- No dependency changes\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-50-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-51-The JSON should contain only stable, language-neutral data: case ID, semantic input DSL, expected canonical hex, expected SHA-256, identity/equivalence group, and explanatory notes. JVM/Node can use the already-pinned `clojure.data.json`; Dart can use `dart:convert`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-52-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-53-Completion criteria:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-54-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-55-- The corpus covers:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-56-  - Map/set insertion order, mixed keys, sorted collections, and duplicate canonical/equality collapse.\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-57-  - List/vector distinction and all four tag-27 names: `dao.jing/list`, `dao.jing/keyword`, `dao.jing/symbol`, and `dao.jing/float64`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-58-  - Metadata retention, reader-position stripping, empty-metadata omission, and symbol metadata.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-59-  - Unicode astral text, noncharacters, composed/decomposed distinction, invalid UTF-8, and unpaired-surrogate rejection.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-60-  - Pathological identifier components, including nil versus empty namespace, literal slashes, whitespace, leading colons, and symbol `\"42\"` versus integer `42`.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-61-  - Byte-string content identity.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-62-  - Integer boundaries and bignums, integer versus integral float, signed zeros, infinities, canonical NaN, float32 widening, decimal scale, reduced ratios, and denominator-one ratios.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-63-  - Malformed frames, tag 39, unknown tags, native CBOR floats, unsupported simple values, duplicate keys/elements, noncanonical encodings, and trailing data.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-64-  - Effective stringref-off, shapes-off, and no-index behavior.\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-65-- Equivalence groups produce identical bytes: integer width, sortedness, sequence realization, stripped/empty metadata, reduced ratios, canonical NaNs, and float32 widening.\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-66-- Retained distinctions produce different bytes: numeric kind, decimal scale, signed zero, retained metadata, and every distinct pathological identifier.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-67-- Pairwise injectivity is asserted over all distinct normalized identities, particularly the complete pathological-identifier class. Both canonical bytes and fixture addresses must differ. SHA-256 collision resistance remains the addressing assumption; it is not presented as mathematical digest injectivity.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-68-- The fixture review records the encoding contract version, dependency pins, generation method, and reviewers.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-69-\n--\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:103:### J2 — Dart codec and carriers\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-104-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-105-Proposed file box:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-106-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-107-- New `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-108-- New `test/dao/jing/cbor_test.cljd`\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-109-- Minimal `:cljd` routing addition to the J1-created facade\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-110-- No edit to `pubspec.yaml` or `pubspec.lock`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-111-- No pre-epic production file changes\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-112-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-113-Completion criteria:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-114-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-115-- Dart reads and reproduces every accepted frozen fixture byte-for-byte.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-116-- Dart rejects the same malformed and out-of-profile fixtures as JVM/Node.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-117-- Explicit Dart carriers cover float64, decimal, and rational values; `BigInt` is used for exact large integers.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-118-- Metadata on codec-constructed collections is cleared before supplied metadata is attached.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-119-- Map/set ordering, equality-collapse checks, strict strings, exact float bits, and profile closure are wrapper-owned.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-120-- Decode followed by strict canonical re-encode catches duplicate-map collapse and encodings the package’s object model cannot preserve.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-121-- Direct portable equality/hash/comparison tests agree with JVM/Node.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-122-- Failure of `cbor` 6.5.1 on a fixture is a stop condition. It must produce a fixture-specific capability report before any hand-rolled parser is considered.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-123-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-124-### J3 — Three-host conformance gate for the unit\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-125-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-126-Proposed file box:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-127-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-128-- New `test/dao/jing/cbor_conformance_test.cljc`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-129-- New `test/dao/jing/cbor_conformance_test.cljd`\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-130-- At most test-only refinements to the frozen fixture loader\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-131-- No production edits\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-132-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-133-Each host should emit a test manifest keyed by fixture ID containing canonical hex, SHA-256, and a normalized semantic signature. Conformance requires equality among JVM, Node, Dart, and the immutable resource.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-134-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-135-Completion criteria:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-136-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-137-- Every host reads the one shared fixture corpus, not a copied host-local table.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-138-- JVM, Node, and Dart produce identical bytes and digests for every supported case.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-139-- An independent raw CBOR-tree inspection confirms tag/name/payload shape and unsigned bytewise ordering without calling the Jing decoder.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-140-- Pairwise injectivity and declared equivalence groups pass on all hosts.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-141-- No test can rewrite the fixture resource.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-142-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-143-Verification lanes:\n--\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:151:The split is deliberately asymmetric: J0 freezes policy, J1 exercises Boring and the hard normalization rules, J2 isolates Dart/package adaptation, and J3 prevents three internally consistent but mutually incompatible implementations from being accepted.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-152-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790