Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-166-- Strict re-encode comparison.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-167-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:168:That is profile normalization, not a hand-rolled CBOR parser. No evidence currently justifies replacing the package with a custom parser. Any hidden failure on the frozen corpus is **UNVERIFIED** until J2 runs; if found, it is a stop-and-review event.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-169-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-170-### Fixture generation and storage: resolved\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-171-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-172-Generate the candidate corpus once using two paths:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-173-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-174-1. Pinned Boring 0.1.30 for candidate output.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-175-2. Independent CBOR-tree construction/inspection from the written contract, without invoking the Jing wrapper.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-176-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-177-Then manually review and commit the literal hex and SHA-256 in `cbor-v1.json`. Runtime tests calculate t