ckage.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md\n\ncbor.cljc is probably large. Let me read it.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Shell access is blocked in this mode, so I'll work from direct file reads (I'll note that `git diff` was unavailable and review the working-tree state against the contract/reports). Let me read the codec, adapters, and Dart writer.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_6a8ef59e5dcc4452ae63cb2d","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_da4c826841404c7495797e27","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc"}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1790032651484,"messageId":"e03f4e55-cb04-46f3-aeb8-f1554d7e1288"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_6a8ef59e5dcc4452ae63cb2d","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 1386 lines\n1: (ns dao.jing.cbor\n2:   \"DaoJing's canonical CBOR value codec and portable numeric operations\n3:    (docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md, phases J1 and J2: JVM, ClojureScript\n4:    and Dart).\n5: \n6:    `encode` turns one supported value into its canonical payload bytes;\n7:    `decode` accepts exactly one canonical payload and returns its value.\n8:    The byte contract is the frozen corpus test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json\n9:    and the rulings in its README; this namespace implements it, it does not\n10:    define it.\n11: \n12:    Encoding normalizes a value into a wire tree (see `dao.jing.cbor.boring`)\n13:    and lets Boring write the bytes:\n14: \n15:    * keywords and symbols: tag 27 `dao.jing/keyword` / `dao.jing/symbol`\n16:      over `[namespace name]`, read from the identifier's fields;\n17:    * lists and finite seqs: tag 27 `dao.jing/list` over the item array;\n18:      vectors are plain arrays;\n19:    * floating point: tag 27 `dao.jing/float64` over eight big-endian bytes,\n20:      float32 widened exactly, every NaN made 7ff8000000000000;\n21:    * integers: CBOR integers, tags 2/3 beyond 64 bits;\n22:    * decimals: tag 4 `[exponent mantissa]`; ratios: tag 30, reduced;\n23:    * sets: tag 258 over elements sorted by their canonical bytes;\n24:    * metadata on collections and symbols: tag 27 `clojure/with-meta` over\n25:      `[meta value]`, outermost, after stripping unqualified :line :column\n26:      :end-line :end-column (validated before stripping) and omitting empty\n27:      metadata.\n28: \n29:    Decoding reads the bytes with Jing's own structural reader, which checks\n30:    every tag, frame name and payload shape before any host conversion (the\n31:    plan's \\\"validate before any lossy host conversion\\\"), then requires the\n32:    decoded value to re-encode to the identical bytes. Boring's decoder is not\n33:    used: its native mappings (tag-30 ratios collapsing denominator 1,\n34:    stringref and date tags, with-meta, a dropped trailing index frame, and\n35:    JavaScript numbers that cannot tell 1.0 from 1) would decide Jing bytes.\n36: \n37:    Every refusal is an ex-info whose data carries `::refusal`, one of the\n38:    corpus refusal classes as a keyword (`:non-canonical`,\n39:    `:unpaired-surrogate`, ...); `refusal` reads it.\n40: \n41:    Numbers: the JVM keeps its native exact kinds (long, BigInt, Double,\n42:    BigDecimal, Ratio) and adds a `Rational` carrier for denominator-1\n43:    ratios. ClojureScript uses safe-integer numbers and BigInt for integers,\n44:    and carriers for float64, decimal and rational content. Host `=` cannot\n45:    compare carriers with native numbers symmetrically, so the portable\n46:    operations are explicit functions: `num=`, `num-hash`, `num-compare`, and\n47:    the recursive `equiv` / `equiv-hash`.\n48: \n49:    Dart (J2): the same reader, profile and portable operations run on\n50:    ClojureDart. The byte writer there is the pinned `cbor` 6.5.1 package\n51:    behind `dao.jing.cbor.cljd`, which implements the same wire vocabulary as\n52:    `dao.jing.cbor.boring`. Dart integers are 64-bit ints and BigInt, floats\n53:    are native doubles (a distinct type from int on the Dart VM), and decimals\n54:    and ratios use the Decimal and Rational carriers. Every host reader\n55:    conditional names `:cljd` first.\"\n56:   (:refer-clojure :exclude [decimal? ratio?])\n57:   (:require\n58:     #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:convert\" :as convert]\n59:                [dao.jing.cbor.cljd :as wire]]\n60:         :default [[dao.jing.cbor.boring :as wire]]))\n61:   #?@(:cljd [(:import\n62:                [\"dart:core\" BigInt FormatException String]\n63:                [\"dart:typed_data\" ByteData Uint8List])]\n64:       :clj [(:import\n65:               (java.math\n66:                 BigDecimal\n67:                 BigInteger)\n68:               (java.nio\n69:                 ByteBuffer)\n70:               (java.nio.charset\n71:                 CharacterCodingException\n72:                 CodingErrorAction\n73:                 StandardCharsets))]))\n74: \n75: \n76: ;; ==========================================================================\n77: ;; Refusals\n78: ;; ==========================================================================\n79: \n80: (defn- refuse\n81:   \"Throw the refusal `cls` (a corpus refusal class keyword).\"\n82:   ([cls] (refuse cls nil))\n83:   ([cls detail]\n84:    (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.jing.cbor refused: \" (name cls)\n85:                         (when detail (str \" (\" detail \")\")))\n86:                    {::refusal cls :detail detail}))))\n87: \n88: \n89: (defn- type-name\n90:   \"The host type of x, for refusal details.\"\n91:   [x]\n92:   #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n93:      :default (str (type x))))\n94: \n95: \n96: (defn refusal\n97:   \"The refusal class keyword of a thrown codec refusal, or nil.\"\n98:   [ex]\n99:   (::refusal (ex-data ex)))\n100: \n101: \n102: ;; ==========================================================================\n103: ;; Exact host big integers: BigInteger on the JVM, BigInt on JavaScript\n104: ;; ==========================================================================\n105: \n106: #?(:cljs\n107:    (defn- bigint?\n108:      [x]\n109:      (identical? \"bigint\" (js* \"typeof ~{}\" x))))\n110: \n111: \n112: (defn- big\n113:   \"An exact host big integer from a host integer or a decimal string.\n114:    Anything else (a float, a non-integral number) is refused loudly\n115:    rather than truncated.\"\n116:   [x]\n117:   #?(:cljd (cond (dart/is? x BigInt) x\n118:                  (dart/is? x int) (BigInt.from x)\n119:                  (string? x) (BigInt.parse x)\n120:                  :else (refuse :unsupported-value\n121:                                (str \"not an exact integer: \" x)))\n122:      :clj (cond (instance? BigInteger x) x\n123:                 (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt x)\n124:                 (.toBigInteger ^clojure.lang.BigInt x)\n125:                 (string? x) (BigInteger. ^String x)\n126:                 (or (instance? Long x) (instance? Integer x)\n127:                     (instance? Short x) (instance? Byte x))\n128:                 (BigInteger/valueOf (long x))\n129:                 :else (refuse :unsupported-value\n130:                               (str \"not an exact integer: \" (type x))))\n131:      :cljs (if (and (number? x) (not (js/Number.isInteger x)))\n132:              (refuse :unsupported-value (str \"not an exact integer: \" x))\n133:              (js/BigInt x))))\n134: \n135: \n136: (def ^:private zero (big 0))\n137: (def ^:private one (big 1))\n138: (def ^:private two (big 2))\n139: (def ^:private ten (big 10))\n140: \n141: \n142: (defn- b+\n143:   [a b]\n144:   #?(:cljd (. ^BigInt a \"+\" b)\n145:      :clj (.add ^BigInteger a ^BigInteger b)\n146:      :cljs (js* \"(~{} + ~{})\" a b)))\n147: \n148: \n149: (defn- b-\n150:   [a b]\n151:   #?(:cljd (. ^BigInt a \"-\" b)\n152:      :clj (.subtract ^BigInteger a ^BigInteger b)\n153:      :cljs (js* \"(~{} - ~{})\" a b)))\n154: \n155: \n156: (defn- b*\n157:   [a b]\n158:   #?(:cljd (. ^BigInt a \"*\" b)\n159:      :clj (.multiply ^BigInteger a ^BigInteger b)\n160:      :cljs (js* \"(~{} * ~{})\" a b)))\n161: \n162: \n163: (defn- bquot\n164:   \"Quotient truncated toward zero.\"\n165:   [a b]\n166:   #?(:cljd (. ^BigInt a \"~/\" b)\n167:      :clj (.divide ^BigInteger a ^BigInteger b)\n168:      :cljs (js* \"(~{} / ~{})\" a b)))\n169: \n170: \n171: (defn- bcmp\n172:   [a b]\n173:   ;; Dart's BigInt.compareTo returns any negative or positive int, not\n174:   ;; just -1 or 1; every host answers exactly -1, 0 or 1.\n175:   #?(:cljd (let [c (.compareTo ^BigInt a b)] (cond (neg? c) -1 (pos? c) 1 :else 0))\n176:      :clj (.compareTo ^BigInteger a ^BigInteger b)\n177:      :cljs (cond (js* \"(~{} < ~{})\" a b) -1\n178:                  (js* \"(~{} > ~{})\" a b) 1\n179:                  :else 0)))\n180: \n181: \n182: (defn- bsign\n183:   [a]\n184:   (bcmp a zero))\n185: \n186: \n187: #?(:cljs\n188:    (defn- brem\n189:      [a b]\n190:      (js* \"(~{} % ~{})\" a b)))\n191: \n192: \n193: #?(:cljs\n194:    (defn- babs\n195:      [a]\n196:      (if (neg? (bsign a)) (b- zero a) a)))\n197: \n198: \n199: (defn- bgcd\n200:   [a b]\n201:   #?(:cljd (.gcd ^BigInt a b)\n202:      :clj (.gcd ^BigInteger a ^BigInteger b)\n203:      :cljs (loop [x (babs a) y (babs b)]\n204:              (if (zero? (bsign y)) x (recur y (brem x y))))))\n205: \n206: \n207: (defn- bpow\n208:   \"base raised to the non-negative host integer n, by squaring.\"\n209:   [base n]\n210:   (loop [result one b base n n]\n211:     (if (zero? n)\n212:       result\n213:       (recur (if (odd? n) (b* result b) result)\n214:              (b* b b)\n215:              (quot n 2)))))\n216: \n217: \n218: (def ^:private two-64 (bpow two 64))\n219: (def ^:private neg-two-64 (b- zero two-64))\n220: \n221: \n222: (defn- b->int\n223:   \"The host integer for exact b: long or BigInt on the JVM, a safe\n224:    integer number or BigInt on JavaScript, a 64-bit int or BigInt on Dart.\"\n225:   [b]\n226:   #?(:cljd (if (.-isValidInt ^BigInt b) (.toInt ^BigInt b) b)\n227:      :clj (if (< (.bitLength ^BigInteger b) 64)\n228:             (.longValue ^BigInteger b)\n229:             (clojure.lang.BigInt/fromBigInteger b))\n230:      :cljs (let [n (js/Number b)]\n231:              (if (js/Number.isSafeInteger n) n b))))\n232: \n233: \n234: (defn- magnitude-bytes\n235:   \"Minimal big-endian bytes of non-negative b; empty for zero.\"\n236:   [b]\n237:   #?(:cljd (let [ff (BigInt.from 255)]\n238:              (loop [b b acc ()]\n239:                (if (zero? (bsign b))\n240:                  (Uint8List.fromList (vec acc))\n241:                  (recur (. ^BigInt b \">>\" 8) (conj acc (.toInt ^BigInt (. ^BigInt b \"&\" ff)))))))\n242:      :clj (let [raw (.toByteArray ^BigInteger b)]\n243:             (if (and (pos? (alength raw)) (zero? (aget raw 0)))\n244:               (java.util.Arrays/copyOfRange raw 1 (alength raw))\n245:               raw))\n246:      :cljs (if (zero? (bsign b))\n247:              (js/Uint8Array. 0)\n248:              (let [h (.toString b 16)\n249:                    h (if (odd? (count h)) (str \"0\" h) h)\n250:                    out (js/Uint8Array. (quot (count h) 2))]\n251:                (dotimes [i (alength out)]\n252:                  (aset out i (js/parseInt (subs h (* 2 i) (+ 2 (* 2 i))) 16)))\n253:                out))))\n254: \n255: \n256: ;; ==========================================================================\n257: ;; Host byte arrays\n258: ;; ==========================================================================\n259: \n260: (defn- blen\n261:   \"The length of a host byte array.\"\n262:   [bs]\n263:   #?(:cljd (.-length ^Uint8List bs)\n264:      :default (alength bs)))\n265: \n266: \n267: (defn- byte-at\n268:   [bs i]\n269:   #?(:cljd (. ^Uint8List bs \"[]\" i)\n270:      :clj (bit-and (aget ^bytes bs i) 0xff)\n271:      :cljs (aget bs i)))\n272: \n273: \n274: (defn- copy-range\n275:   [bs start end]\n276:   #?(:cljd (Uint8List.fromList (.sublist ^Uint8List bs start end))\n277:      :clj (java.util.Arrays/copyOfRange ^bytes bs (int start) (int end))\n278:      :cljs (.slice bs start end)))\n279: \n280: \n281: (defn- span-big\n282:   \"Unsigned big-endian integer of bs[start, end).\"\n283:   [bs start end]\n284:   (loop [i start acc zero]\n285:     (if (= i end)\n286:       acc\n287:       (recur (inc i) (b+ (b* acc (big 256)) (big (byte-at bs i)))))))\n288: \n289: \n290: (defn- span-key\n291:   \"A string naming the exact bytes bs[start, end), for duplicate checks.\"\n292:   [bs start end]\n293:   (apply str (map #(let [b (byte-at bs %)]\n294:                      (str (when (< b 16) \"0\")\n295:                           #?(:cljd (.toRadixString ^int b 16)\n296:                              :clj (Integer/toHexString b)\n297:                              :cljs (.toString b 16))))\n298:                   (range start end))))\n299: \n300: \n301: (defn- bytes-hex\n302:   [bs]\n303:   (span-key bs 0 (blen bs)))\n304: \n305: \n306: (defn- bytes=\n307:   [a b]\n308:   (let [n (blen a)]\n309:     (and (= n (blen b))\n310:          (loop [i 0]\n311:            (or (= i n)\n312:                (and (= (byte-at a i) (byte-at b i))\n313:                     (recur (inc i))))))))\n314: \n315: \n316: ;; ==========================================================================\n317: ;; Numeric kinds and carriers\n318: ;; ==========================================================================\n319: \n320: #?(:cljs\n321:    (defn- neg-zero?\n322:      [x]\n323:      (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1 x)))))\n324: \n325: \n326: #?(:cljs\n327:    (defn- double-bits-hex\n328:      \"The 16 hex digits of a JS number's IEEE-754 bits.\"\n329:      [d]\n330:      (let [view (js/DataView. (js/ArrayBuffer. 8))]\n331:        (.setFloat64 view 0 d)\n332:        (apply str (map #(let [b (.getUint8 view %)]\n333:   