1562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-135-Completion criteria:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-136-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-137-- Every host reads the one shared fixture corpus, not a copied host-local table.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-138-- JVM, Node, and Dart produce identical bytes and digests for every supported case.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-139-- An independent raw CBOR-tree inspection confirms tag/name/payload shape and unsigned bytewise ordering without calling the Jing decoder.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-140-- Pairwise injectivity and declared equivalence groups pass on all hosts.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-141-- No test can rewrite the fixture resource.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-142-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-143-Verification lanes:\n--\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:151:The split is deliberately asymmetric: J0 freezes policy, J1 exercises Boring and the hard normalization rules, J2 isolates Dart/package adaptation, and J3 prevents three internally consistent but mutually incompatible implementations from being accepted.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-152-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-153-## 3. Decisions I need from you, resolved where possible\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-154-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-155-### Dart route: resolved — use `cbor` 6.5.1\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-156-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-157-The maintained-package route is viable. The pinned package exposes arbitrary tags, `BigInt`, decimal fractions, rational numbers, definite containers, and strict string conversion. [pub.dev API](https://pub.dev/documentation/cbor/latest/cbor/)\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-158-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-159-The Jing wrapper must still implement profile policy:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-160-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-161-- Canonical map/set ordering.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-162-- Duplicate and equality-collapse rejection.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-163-- Closed accepted-tag vocabulary.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-164-- Exact IEEE-754 payload handling.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-165-- Surrogate validation.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-166-- Strict re-encode comparison.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-167-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:168:That is profile normalization, not a hand-rolled CBOR parser. No evidence currently justifies replacing the package with a custom parser. Any hidden failure on the frozen corpus is **UNVERIFIED** until J2 runs; if found, it is a stop-and-review event.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-169-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-170-### Fixture generation and storage: resolved\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-171-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-172-Generate the candidate corpus once using two paths:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-173-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-174-1. Pinned Boring 0.1.30 for candidate output.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-175-2. Independent CBOR-tree construction/inspection from the written contract, without invoking the Jing wrapper.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-176-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-177-Then manually review and commit the literal hex and SHA-256 in `cbor-v1.json`. Runtime tests calculate the digest from frozen hex and compare implementations against it; they never update it.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-178-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-179-An upgrade may run against the frozen corpus but may not regenerate it. Changing a byte requires:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-180-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-181-- A new explicit contract version or reviewed correction.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-182-- A written case-by-case byte delta.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-183-- Architect approval.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-184-- Independent different-family review.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-185-- No overwrite mode in ordinary tests or build scripts.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-186-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-187-A developer-only candidate generator, if useful, should print to stdout or an untracked temporary path and have no command capable of overwriting the frozen resource.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-188-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-189-### Effective Boring options: resolved by code inspection plus fixtures\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-190-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-191-For Boring 0.1.30, `:profile :canonical` locks canonical encoding, string references off, and shapes off; conflicting overrides throw. Normal `boring/encode` emits one item, while indexed encoding is a separate operation. Thus the plan’s option-precedence concern is partly stale for this pin.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-192-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-193-The contract must nevertheless prove effects, not trust option names:\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-194-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-195-- Repeated strings stay ordinary text rather than string references.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-196-- Record-like/repeated structures do not produce shape tables.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-197-- Exact parsing consumes one value and reaches EOF, with no index/trailing frame.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-198-- Canonical map/set fixtures prove the required unsigned bytewise ordering.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-199-- Tests deliberately pass conflicting settings where the API permits and require rejection rather than changed bytes.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-200-- The implementation calls the ordinary encoder, never the indexed API.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-201-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-202-### Owning role: resolved\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-203-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-204-The primary owner is the **DaoSpace & DaoJing Storage Engineer**, whose charter covers content-addressed storage and Jing. The QA/Verification Engineer owns the cross-host verification review, not the implementation. The Stream/Transport Engineer does not become an implementation owner until step 4.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-205-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-206-## 4. Routing recommendation\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-207-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-208-Implementation should begin after the Claude pool refresh at 2026-09-22 04:00 +07.\n--\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:214:| J2 Dart codec | Claude Opus 5 | GLM-5.3 | GPT architect confirms package viability and parity |\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-215-| J3 conformance | Claude Sonnet 5 | Gemini 3.1 Pro High | GPT architect accepts the complete steps 1–2 unit |\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-216-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:217:GLM-5.3 is best reserved for one bounded J2 static/adversarial review because it is already around 68% usage and does not reset until 2026-09-27. J2 benefits most from a reviewer independent of both the Claude implementation and the JVM-centered reference path.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-218-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-219-Every phase should follow the repository loop: implementer produces the scoped diff and evidence; different-family reviewer issues findings; the same implementer fixes them; the reviewer resumes; GPT performs the architecture sign-off at the stated boundary.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-220-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-221-This report is the pre-implementation architect clearance for J0–J3 only. It does not authorize step 3 or either owner gate.\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-222-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-223-## 5. The owner gate checklist\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-224-\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-225-### Gate 1 — `dao.space` numeric semantics\n/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/collab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-226-\ncollab/1790011562103-architect-jing-cbor-work-package.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md-227