classify as P2 (critical gap: the rationale for Dart skips on 2 frozen cases cites an errata row that does not yet exist; ratification of the Dart column is required before commit) — or P3. Given this project's strictness (\"skip only by id and with rationale\" tied to README/errata), and given that J1's sign-off made E1 authoritative, the absence of an authoritative Dart row means the two Dart skips currently lack ratified justification. That's P2 (must be fixed by errata addition before commit — orchestrator/architect action, not a code change).\n\nHmm, but the brief says \"the implementer proposes a Dart column to the errata E1 table (signed-zero and vector-list N/A on Dart, all others live): validate against code\". So my job: confirm the proposal matches code. It does. The errata addition itself is pending orchestrator. Record validation + P2 (blocker on commit) as an action item.\n\nNext let me check the README obligations for js-unsafe-integer and non-ASCII. Also confirm whether `coll/map-both-slash-keywords` is canonical and check the README's Dart note.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Checking the README obligations, non-ASCII scan of the changed files, and a few corpus ids.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_13b3fc5f5fb0415a969aa3dc","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"js-unsafe-integer|Obligations","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.README.md","output_mode":"content","-C":6}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a14feed700bb4fc48c0ec497","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"[^\\x00-\\x7F]","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-jing-cbor/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc","output_mode":"content"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_e0bf396c7e4943d298879811","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\"id\": \"coll/(map-both-slash-keywords|set-signed-zero-collapse|set-vector-list-collapse|map-integer-width-duplicate|set-decimal-scale-collapse|set-nan-payload-duplicate|map-nan-payload-duplicate)\"","path":"/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-