longer strings, 8-byte heads (rare). No issue.\n\n**Subtle issue J — `frame`: `(str tag-symbol)`. In cljd, `str` on a symbol gives the name with ns ✓. But could cljd's symbol str escape anything? 'dao.jing/float64 → \"dao.jing/float64\" ✓. 'clojure/with-meta ✓.\n\n**Subtle issue K — the shared encoder calls `wire/frame 'dao.jing/list (mapv ...)`, payload is a vector of nodes → `content-node` → `array-node` ✓. For float64 frames the payload is Uint8List → CborBytes ✓.\n\n**Subtle issue L — `tagged 258` inside set-wire: `(wire/tagged 258 (mapv second (sort-by first wired)))` — vector of nodes → CborList with tag ✓ fixed length ✓.\n\n**Subtle issue M — `tagged 4` for decimal: `(wire/tagged 4 [(int-wire ...) (int-wire ...)])` — vector of two nodes ✓.\n\n**Subtle issue N — `tagged 2/3` with Uint8List → `.tags`ed CborBytes ✓.\n\n**Dart reader traps — `case (int major)`: `int` on BigInt? For ai 27, major is small so always int. OK. But `(case (int v)` inside item->value :simple — v is int ✓.\n\n**`deep!` on BigInt depth? None.\n\n**`read-head` ai 24-26 reduce: on Dart `byte-at` returns int ✓; acc ≤ 2^32-1 ✓.\n\n**`(= 0xff (byte-at bs pos))` ✓.\n\n**`(str e)` inside utf8 catch — e is FormatException ✓.\n\n**`(catch FormatException e ...)` — cljd's catch with type annotation ✓. But does the Dart code for `utf8` throw other exception types? `String.fromCharCode` no. `.convert` only throws FormatException on malformed (RangeError if start/end are invalid — can't happen).\n\nHmm wait — one more point about the Dart code for utf8: `(try (.convert (convert/Utf8Decoder.) bs at end) ...)` — `bs` here is the full Uint8List, `at`/`end` are indices. ✓.\n\nBut there's a subtle bug candidate: **what if `at > end`?** Can't happen.\n\n**BOM loop when a BOM straddles chunk boundaries in indefinite-length text**: chunk-level utf8 call per chunk. If the sequence is split mid-chunk, the first chunk's decode fails → :invalid-utf8 ✓ (desired: indefinite text will be refused as non-canonical on 